OL,3,AX-planes: Are they needed in the new
OL,4,Aera of drones?
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere's a weird and wonderful jet
OL,7,Fflying over the US. It has the nose of
OL,8,Fanteater, parts cannibalised from other
OL,9,Fplanes and a cockpit so far back the
OL,10,Fpilot depends on a camera to see where
OL,11,Fhe's going.
OL,13,FThis contraption, the X-59, might just
OL,14,Fbe the future of air travel.
OL,16,FThe X-59's owes its eccentric design to
OL,17,Fthe problem of sonic booms. The
OL,18,Fshockwave created by a jet breaking the
OL,19,Fsound barrier restricted Concorde to
OL,20,Fflights over the sea and barred it from
OL,21,Flucrative routes across the US.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,109,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790353094
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AX-planes: Are they needed in the new
OL,4,Aera of drones?
OL,5,
OL,6,FNow Nasa is working around that problem
OL,7,Fusing the X-59's elongated snout to
OL,8,Fflatten supersonic booms into tolerable
OL,9,Fbumps in the background.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/19
